{{Quote|Welcome to the House of Rylanz.|Enza Rylanz to Cassian Andor|<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" />}}
The '''House of Rylanz''' was a [[twillery]] located in [[Palmo]], the [[capital]] [[city]] of [[Ghorman]]. The store was sold the fabric known as [[Ghorman twill]] made from [[Ghorman silk]].<ref name="Episode highlights">{{SW|url=news/andor-explained-season-2-highlights-episodes-4-5-6|text=''Andor'' Explained: Episodes 4-6 - "Ever Been to Ghorman?", "I Have Friends Everywhere", and "What a Festive Evening"}}</ref> In [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Friends Timeline">"[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]" establishes that the events of "[[I Have Friends Everywhere]]" take place in [[3 BBY]].</ref> the twillery was run by [[Carro Rylanz]] and had been in his family for nineteen generations. It was one of the youngest twilleries in Palmo. The webberie estates that supplied the House of Rylanz were quite far away from the capital.<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" /> 

During this year, [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] visited the twillery's show room under the alias Varian Skye, a [[Coruscanti]] [[fashion designer]] making his first pilgrimage to Ghorman to see the fabrics crafted at the House of Rylanz. In reality Andor was there to meet with Carro and evaluate the [[Ghorman Front]], a the local rebel cell run by Rylanz. Due to the competitive nature of twilleries the House of Rylanz was able to sweep for [[listening device]]s daily without raising suspicion. This allowed Andor and Carro to discuss the Front's rebel plans.<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" />

==Behind the scenes==
House of Rylanz appeared in the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', first appearing in the seasons's fifth episode, "[[I Have Friends Everywhere]]," which was released on [[Disney+]]<ref name="I Have Friends Everywhere" /> on [[April 22]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref>

